NAME
       c2c-proxy - the conventions of the relay, and the wire it rides

DESCRIPTION
       The proxy is the relay between the harness and the front. It
       rides the OpenAI wire, and it keeps the following conventions:

       Routes
              /v1/ is the prefix of the stable. Everything under it is
              as published; what is not published is not promised.

       The pair in the model name
              "model": "c2c/RECEIVER+SHARER" names the fusion. Without
              the plus, the receiver speaks alone — the relay becomes a
              plain proxy, and the wire carries text only.

       The stream
              With "stream": true the answer is carried in server-sent
              events, one completion, a chunk, delta by delta, ending
              with data: [DONE]. The token that arrives is the token of
              the receiver, the cache of the sharer already fused.

       The authentication
              authorization: bearer KEY. The key is compared in
              constant time. No key, no gate — but bind the host to
              127.0.0.1 then, and count the cost.

WIRE FORMAT OF THE CACHE ENVELOPE
       The cache on the wire is a mapping::

           {"receiver": NAME, "sharer": NAME, "revision": N,
            "num_layers": N, "num_heads": N, "num_key_value_heads": N,
            "head_size": N, "hidden_size": N,
            "layers": [{"layer": N, "key": TENSOR, "value": TENSOR}]}

       The geometry is checked against the manifest of the pair before
       the tensor is trusted: a cache that lies about its geometry is
       refused, not fused.

ENVIRONMENT
       C2C_PROXY_HOST, C2C_PROXY_PORT, C2C_API_KEY, C2C_PAIRS,
       C2C_FUSE_ALWAYS — as in c2c.config(5), read once, at the start
       of the relay.

SEE ALSO
       c2c(1), c2c-serve(1), c2c.config(5), c2c-engines(7)

